{"kind":"report","text":"# Shared room name and local room selection\n\n2026-10-09. Specification for request 07eee7f6939fe0854003d7531715b12b919694c2, actual promise 9a58928b782cbaefad88642ed016d8044531bd90. Source read at accepted main 38b0b2f2bdb7af6f59076ac3b423741555a7b437. Inherited stale-base status is disclosed. Hugh chose a shared name managed by authorized members, separate from the generated repository name. This note proposes the smallest contract/source slice; it adopts nothing, executes no app/provider, changes no source and runs no tests. Page actions/list request 12cc35cd remains independent.\n\n## Current truth\n\nThe room is its native directory scope/reference and recorded register/claim, membership (including incarnation), rules and destination relationships. The directory's one `repository` item holds a FIXED repository descriptor and branch; generated repository name is part of that descriptor. Changing presentation must not rename that repository or change any scope ID/incarnation, branch, URLs, references, actor identity or signing target.\n\nPage `Room.name` currently reads that generated repository name, not a shared friendly name. The typed Create room name is a browser-local label associated with its place/register; it is not native metadata. The switcher opens Settings. Settings retains only the selected room/key context; there is no enrolled-room catalog or shared-name act/read. Directory @1/@2 have no mutable friendly-name item/slot or rename act. Membership has no room-name action. Existing `membership.manage` (admin baseline) manages members/keys/role action lists; it is not already authority to rename a room. `rules.publish`, `change.edit-any` and local key possession are likewise not room-name authority.\n\n## Proposed contract, requiring exact review/adoption\n\nKeep the directory as the authority for room metadata. In a NEW pinned directory definition, create one separate `room-profile` item at genesis, with optional mutable `displayName`, and a signed transition tentatively named `set-room-name`. A separate item avoids concurrent issue-number updates to the repository item causing unrelated rename conflicts. The act names the actual profile item and expected revision, takes only bounded name text, and changes only that display-name slot. No external operation, repository write, key change, relation update or side effect. Empty-after-trim means unnamed/clear, under the same authority; do not overload absent metadata with unreadable state. These names/schema are proposals, not current APIs.\n\nUse a dedicated action tentatively `room.name`; grant authority through the room's real membership reference and current active member/key observation under existing authority windows. Proposed initial default: admin only; an admin may explicitly authorize additional human roles through the existing whole-list `set-actions` mechanism once the action/definition is adopted. Do not equate “authorized members” with all members, all maintainers or all keys. The exact default role policy is an owner decision; agent/checker renaming is excluded from the initial human interface and must not become implicit via a broad grant. Do not infer grant ownership from email, shared name, local enrollment label or repository access. Local controls use actual held action; backend authority decides if membership/key/role changes during a request.\n\nBounds proposed for adoption: name after explicit confirmation of trimming is well-formed Unicode, at most 256 UTF-8 bytes, single line, with C0/DEL controls and line separators rejected; empty means clear. Show the exact saved result in confirmation; no hidden Unicode normalization or truncation. Names are nonunique presentation, never routing identities. Duplicate names require a secondary repository/short-ID disambiguator. DOM text/attribute APIs render names literally; never interpolate HTML, CSS selectors or URL paths. Long/multibyte and bidirectional names must not obscure the immutable identity; use isolated text and wrapping, while retaining full ID in inspection.\n\nConcurrent renames use the existing item expected-revision mechanism. A and B read profile revision r; first admitted change increments it, second receives native `revision-moved` with `judgedAt`. Preserve B's proposed text and show old/current/proposed names; only deliberate reload/compare/reconfirmation signs another request. Never silently last-write-wins/re-sign. Accepted rename is a native entry/receipt with actor, name and effects. For the proposed ordinary naming act, native `ScopeCore.submit` returns an `Answer.refused` (including `revision-moved`) with reason/`judgedAt` through its answer branch, without writing a rename entry or receipt; retain that response in the client task record. This does not mean every kind of refusal is unwritten: genesis refusal and recorded operation/outcome refusal can be history entries, and a submit turn can separately drain due work. Do not promise a native audit entry for the rejected rename itself. History of accepted names is native entry history, not a new audit subsystem.\n\n## Reading and cross-device observation\n\nThe minimum read surface is the existing authenticated directory summary/item/entry/history shapes, extended only by the adopted definition's actual profile item/slot. Page must expose separately `sharedName`, its actual directory/profile identity/revision and sampled head, versus `repositoryName` and optional `personalLabel`. Read the full current name by the real room's established session/signed-read authority; an unauthenticated/revoked/unreadable response is unavailable, never unnamed, local default or a previously cached name presented as current. No public Site route or new cross-device catalog is implied.\n\nAnother enrolled member/device independently reads that same directory item and sees the same name at the same head/revision, without copying the first device's settings or secret. A later refresh reads a later head; the prior read is a sampled observation, not an ongoing freshness guarantee. Current `RoomOpening` caches an opened room by context, so implementation needs deliberate invalidation/refresh for rename and return/focus/status checks; do not keep a cached shared name indefinitely as authoritative. Cross-device watches/push and durable discovery remain existing identity/continuity owner work, not prerequisites for a truthful manual refresh.\n\nDisplay a verified shared name as primary, generated repository name separately. If the profile is authoritatively unnamed, use “Unnamed room” with repository/short ID; if old pinned definition lacks the feature, say shared naming unavailable for that room, with generated repository/short-ID fallback. If observation is stale/disconnected, label “Last read name” and head/time status; if unavailable with no retained read, use room ID, never a forged shared label. Revoked/unauthorized users get no rename control; refusal remains authoritative even if a stale UI once displayed it.\n\n## Local labels and direct selector\n\nPreserve old local labels as explicitly **Personal label on this browser**; never publish them automatically at migration/claim/join. In UI place them secondarily so they cannot masquerade as authoritative shared names. An authorized person can deliberately copy a personal label into the native shared-name confirmation. Existing typed Create room name remains personal until the shared-name act is actually adopted/admitted; founding plus rename is two separate steps/results, not an atomic promise. Successful founding with failed/unknown naming leaves one existing unnamed room and a retained naming task; no second founding or rollback. No secret transfer is required for this metadata.\n\nDirect selection may list ONLY contexts actually retained on this origin with evidence of successful native enrollment/founding and subsequent validated directory/membership observation. A pasted invitation/config alone or a name match is not enrollment. The smallest local registry is bounded (proposed 64 entries), origin-bound, keyed by full directory reference and membership incarnation plus device-key ID, with actual register/reference provenance where available, recorded membership handle, latest verified public metadata and a local credential reference. No private keys/config/invitation secrets in URLs, labels or public registry metadata; do not copy keys to support a picker. Current raw-secret Page custody is a baseline discrepancy, not permission to implement C4's broader key redesign here. Reuse its selected credential through existing custody until that owner supplies the reviewed device-key abstraction.\n\nCurrent Page Place stores a directory ID rather than its full incarnation; the proposed registry must capture and retain the actual `Summary.scope` full reference from the authenticated directory read and match it on return, never synthesize an incarnation from the ID. Migrate only the current verified selected context, after an authenticated read; do not synthesize entries from archives/labels alone. Successful future Join/founding may add a bounded entry only after actual acceptance and identity observation, without exposing private claim journals. Never evict a context containing unresolved work just to meet a list bound; report full and require deliberate user management, preserving unresolved records. A device learns no rooms it has not retained/enrolled into; this is a local list, not same-member server discovery.\n\nWhen a person selects an entry, revalidate origin, full directory incarnation, directory's actual membership reference, original key ID/current credential, active member/key standing and read session/authority. Preserve the current selection until the chosen context has been verified and settings readback succeeds. Foreign/stale incarnation, unknown key, removed member or revoked key is unavailable/access lost; do not silently select another key/member or run Join. A remembered entry remains inspectable as inaccessible, not permission. Duplicate names use immutable disambiguators. Each room retains its own filters/drafts/pending tasks; switching must not reuse an old room's route/action/authority or erase original unknown results. No implicit cross-origin selection.\n\n## Rename waiting, refusal and uncertainty\n\nBind the naming task to original origin/directory/profile revision/full membership/member/key and frozen text. Retain exact signed envelope and full known answer BEFORE awaited refresh; this is a bounded client change, since current `data.act` does not expose its envelope. Double click and redraw/navigation must not sign a second intent. Check original context immediately before POST. Before-send failure says “Nothing sent”; definite refusal shows reason/head and preserves text; accepted receipt with failed refresh says “Name recorded; current read unavailable”. Do not show the proposed text as current until authenticated resulting read/receipt-following verifies it.\n\nTransport/malformed/lost reply, unavailable or mismatch after POST means “Naming outcome unknown”; preserve original envelope and stop replacement signatures for that task. Existing exact settle/followReceipt can find acceptance; absence is not terminal absence under current `Settlement = Read\u003cReceipt\u003e`. Explicit supported resend uses the same bytes/target, never a fresh idempotency key. Another context's later reply cannot overwrite this known result. Disconnection shows last verified name and draft separately; it grants no rename authority and does not queue an optimistic server change. Reload recovery and the settlement/preparation gap remain owned by existing B2/continuity work: disclose memory-only retention if that is the delivered boundary; do not claim a generic durable outbox.\n\n## Smallest delivery and ownership after adoption\n\n1. Planner/authority/platform owners review and adopt exact metadata item/act/grant/bounds/default-role/clear semantics, plus platform-version compatibility. Every current directory pins @1/@2 at genesis; platform code explicitly preserves old versions. New cohort can receive the proposed profile, but there is no inspected directory-upgrade act. Existing-room support therefore needs an explicit adopted migration/metadata-ownership mechanism that preserves stable room identity, or an honest first release limited to newly founded supporting rooms. Do not mutate old pinned bytes or re-found old rooms to enable a name. A separate new metadata scope is an alternative only with independently adopted linkage/authority; not invented here.\n2. Builder delivers the minimal platform/contract/pinned cohort metadata change and focused native authority/concurrency/read/replay evidence; generic authenticated summary/history transports already exist and should not be duplicated. If a new default membership action is chosen, version/cohort compatibility and old roster policy changes must be explicit, never automatic privilege widening.\n3. Page/025/027 implements separate shared/repository/personal presentation, bounded rename task, fresh reads and local selector using actual supported contexts. Coordinate interfaces with independent **12cc35cd** forms/list delivery; do not block or enlarge that branch. Existing C4 identity owner **18815307e6c306d63766230ed7eb7ddbf94d1f21** supplies device-key/enrollment/discovery/revocation custody; C1/C3/C5/C6 connected-story owners retain trusted authority, retained settlement, continuity UI and deployed two-device acceptance. Shared naming is not completion of those obligations.\n\nDecisions requiring adoption: initial rename roles (admin-default proposal), exact name bounds/clear semantics, existing pinned-room migration versus new-cohort-only release, and local-registry credential interface. Hugh's shared-versus-personal choice is already answered; do not ask it again. None of these authorize repository renaming or a global room catalog.\n\n## Acceptance cases\n\n- Two real enrolled members/devices read the same native shared name/revision/head; rename receipt/history is attributable and replayable. Repository descriptor/name, branch, stable scope IDs/incarnations and all signing targets remain identical. Old personal label never appears as shared or auto-publishes.\n- Only actual held naming action admits rename; unauthorized/removed/revoked key and role changed between UI read and POST refuse. Existing read revocation is respected despite cache. Agent/checker/default-member exclusion matches adopted policy; delegated authority is not implied by local labels.\n- Two concurrent renames from r produce one accepted result and one `revision-moved`, not overwrite; losing draft/current comparison remains usable. Rejected rename submit answer is client-retained, not misreported as a rename entry; independently recorded refused genesis/outcomes remain visible as native history. Boundary Unicode, escaping, controls, empty/unnamed and duplicate-name disambiguation match adopted rules.\n- Wrong directory/member incarnation, foreign origin, merely pasted config/invitation and mismatched/retired key cannot activate a picker entry or rename another room. Switching revalidates real member authority and storage success, preserves original pending/unknown work and separate room query/drafts. Unsupported pinned directories honestly lack the naming feature.\n- Double click/lost reply/refresh failure/context switch preserve exact envelope/known result without replacement signature or false saved name. Accepted naming plus unreadable refresh remains recorded/unavailable; nonterminal settle absence never clears unknown. After disconnect, stale read/draft/new proposal remain distinct. Naming failure after founding never creates a duplicate room.\n- Local selector shows only retained verified contexts, capacity/full/inaccessible cases truthfully; no cross-device/global catalog or secret-bearing URLs. Actual 320px/desktop keyboard task demonstrates shared name, repository name and personal label distinctions. A separate device reads through its own enrollment, not copied secret. Use focused meaningful native/DOM/browser witnesses and one exact-head gate when implementation is commissioned; physical-phone/AT and deployed continuity claims require their owners' actual acceptance.\n\nSource evidence (main 38b0b2f): packages/platform/src/directory.ts:157-185 fixed descriptor and native identity relationships; :220-305 genesis/acts (no name act); packages/platform/src/index.ts:94-115 pinned-version preservation; membership.ts:119-139 baseline grants, :487-493 set-actions, :787-855 authoritative current standing; packages/page/src/data.ts:224-246 directory/membership/name read; main.ts:35-79 one selected Settings/local label, :119-125 local/generated display and Settings switcher, :212-244 context/pre-POST fence, :270-303 save/readback; shell.ts:28-57 context/cache/memory fence; view.ts:10-15 inert DOM; packages/cli/src/commands.ts:219-230 expected revisions; derive/src/judge.ts:288-302 bad-intent/revision-moved; contract/src/intent.ts:40 and result.ts:14-34 signed revision/refusal semantics; scope/src/core.ts:593-637 submit write-versus-refused answer branch; client/src/handle.ts:59-62 settle/submit and followReceipt. Read Plan005 Story3, Plan006 existing owners, Plan027-03 dependencies, B2 settlement gap; FULL-read requests 07eee and C4 18815307 plus disposition 0ff2e4b6. No secret/envelope/user input captured in this note.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9a58928b782cbaefad88642ed016d8044531bd90 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:00a6f83a0f12d69721bf0bd026b14608ffac8a31, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0148a0176116a4fb5401c96dbbb813a144b65616, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0357a3c97289e2782ff1264563897f39ecb2ce42, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03f7bc46d133f1cde1f7936baaaa690a99416b97 and 56 more"}}